{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787548188759035001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"unequaled-waiting-lunamoth","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"b037bce061cd357eb56c7c5a6b26db7caa934d7749ed027c23467544cbf356c7","event_uuid":"5ca1551f-4d3d-4d6b-9b23-5cb2c9194316","position":{"commit_sha":"eff38168682ef410d49e62e047c3812f2f89f0c9","position":"1787544121367922001-5ca1551f-4d3d-4d6b-9b23-5cb2c9194316"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"dee5efc72c996d469fd8584a69456642ad3457acdddd901c5f47ddd28216f3ac","event_uuid":"46a924fe-1b0d-4c80-ab82-5e2a725db2f1","position":{"commit_sha":"e2ad394cf41a4cf90d77387acb9a088f8d31ea44","position":"1787544142388486001-46a924fe-1b0d-4c80-ab82-5e2a725db2f1"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787544121367922001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"46a924fe-1b0d-4c80-ab82-5e2a725db2f1","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"8c8a-2756-ecfa-4b90"}],"description":"## Residual resilience gap (Step-7 follow-up, discovered_from bug 8c8a)\n\nBug 8c8a fixed the DISPOSITION-DROP defect: a retryable provider outage\nmid-run in the completion gate now surfaces as exit 11 (\"transient — retry\")\ninstead of a verdict-less exit-1 hard fault. That is the correct behavior for a\nTRANSIENT outage.\n\nIt does NOT address a separate, deeper resilience gap that the 8c8a\ninvestigation surfaced (see the first RCA comment on 8c8a, the \"banked\nprogress\" analysis): when a completion verify run has BANKED per-criterion\nprogress and then hits a SUSTAINED (non-transient) provider outage, the gate\nstill fails closed to \"could not run\" (now exit 11) rather than DEGRADING to an\nactionable deterministic verdict from the criterion bank via the existing\nno-LLM finalizer. The module docstring at\nsrc/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_recovery.py:11-12 states the design intent:\n\"a deterministic no-LLM fallback so a run with any banked progress can never die\nverdict-less.\" A sustained outage with a non-empty bank still does not honor\nthat invariant.\n\n### Why this is a SEPARATE ticket (not folded into 8c8a)\n- 8c8a's fix is behavior-preserving for the fail-closed posture (never\n  uncertified-closes, never fabricates a certifiable verdict). Adding a\n  banked-degrade path is a NEW behavior with its own certifiability question\n  (a degrade verdict is certifiable=False and must NOT auto-close a ticket —\n  see close_precheck.py:696-704), so it needs its own plan review and design.\n- Folding it into the bug would exceed the bugfix-size floor and mask the\n  narrow, provable disposition-plumbing fix.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] A completion verify run with a NON-EMPTY criterion bank that hits a\n      sustained provider outage finalizes a deterministic BLOCK/FAIL verdict\n      from the bank (no additional LLM calls), honoring \"can never die\n      verdict-less\".\n- [ ] The degrade verdict is certifiable=False and does NOT close the subject\n      ticket without an operator decision (no uncertified auto-close).\n- [ ] An EMPTY-bank sustained outage keeps the current retryable exit-11\n      posture (nothing to degrade to).\n- [ ] RED->GREEN with a held-out oracle + defect-seeded mutation.\n\n### Chronic-area context\nThis is the transport instance of a recurring theme (gates failing closed to an\nun-actionable \"could not run\" instead of degrading to a verdict) tracked across\n46a2/3211/0707/10ae/61d8 and a live cluster of OPEN llm-degrade session_logs.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["llm-degrade","completion-gate","resilience","future-work"],"ticket_id":"b39a-8770-a8b2-459a","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Completion gate: degrade to banked verdict on sustained provider outage","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["5ca1551f-4d3d-4d6b-9b23-5cb2c9194316","46a924fe-1b0d-4c80-ab82-5e2a725db2f1"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787548188759035001,"uuid":"0a59aaa0-c761-4ea8-b55f-d3a5a0d33b8b"}